{
  "slug": "artist:paul-oakenfold",
  "name": "Paul Oakenfold",
  "editorial_article": "Born in 1963 in London, Paul Oakenfold rose to prominence in the early 1980s as a club DJ before becoming a central figure in the trance scene. His extensive discography includes studio efforts like the 2002 album Bunkka and numerous mixes such as the 1997 Global Underground 004 and 1998's Tranceport. Beyond his work as a solo artist and DJ, Oakenfold has helmed the Perfecto Records label and produced soundtracks for films including Swordfish, The Bourne Identity, and Collateral. He is known for prolific remixing, having provided reworks for artists ranging from Madonna and Britney Spears to Daft Punk and Hans Zimmer. Oakenfold's career also features significant collaborations across genres, including tracks with Aloe Blacc, Zhu, and Pharrell, as well as production work for TV themes like the Big Brother UK music.",
